  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Academy of Culinary Arts Cambodia II - kvalificerad yrkesutbildning</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Academy of Culinary Arts Cambodia II - vocational training - Vocational education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att konsolidera uppbyggandet av yrkesh&#xf6;gskola av internationell standard f&#xf6;r bes&#xf6;ksindustrin. Yrkesh&#xf6;gskolan drivs i entreprenadformen Offentlig Privat Samverkan (OPS), representerad av den kambodjanska staten i form av ministerierna f&#xf6;r finans, turism och handel och det privata n&#xe4;ringslivet i form av bes&#xf6;ksn&#xe4;ringens organisationer. Fr&#xe5;n givarsidan samfinansieras insatsen av Sida och andra bist&#xe5;ndsorganisationer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention consolidates the creation of a vocational institute of international standard for the hospitality sector. The institute is established in the form of a Public-Private-Partnership (PPP), represented by the Cambodian Government in the form of the Ministries of Finance, Tourism and Commerce and the private sector represented by the hospitality sector&#x2019;s associations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the intervention is to contribute to the development of a sustainable and equitable labour market, through providing high quality training to young Cambodian men and women. The secondary objective is to provide the hospitality industry with qualified, trained and certified professionals through high quality and innovative educational programmes that ensure that the students possess valuable transferable skills in all aspects of culinary competencies. 
The intervention consolidates the creation of a vocational institute of international standard for the hospitality sector. The institute is established in the form of a PPP, the public part represented by the Cambodian Government in the form of the ministries of labour, tourism, commerce and education and the private part by enterprises in the hospitality sector.</narrative>
  </description>
